  "pass_a_gloss": "[Stephen's prayer continues] … the souls of the righteous enter; no longer do the gloomy places of death receive the spirits of the living. After you, who became at once firstfruits of the living and of the dead [1 Corinthians 15:20], so that you might be Lord of both dead and living [Romans 14:9], the lump of all the dead takes courage, not without reason. 'Receive, then, my spirit' [Acts 7:59]. Do not allow the hunters to lie in wait for your sparrow [Psalm 123:7 LXX], nor the enemies who meet me at the gates to ruin my going away from the earth, nor to disturb for me the way up into the heavens. §27 But this prayer he sacrificed for himself, and another again for the people of the Jews: 'Lord, do not set for them this sin' [Acts 7:60]. And … [the sentence continues in the next section]",
  "pass_b_english": [
    "“…souls of the righteous enter; no longer do the gloomy regions of death take in the spirits of the living. Following you, who became at once the firstfruits of the living and of the dead (1 Corinthians 15:20), so that you might be Lord of both the dead and the living (Romans 14:9), the whole mass of the dead takes courage, and not without reason.",
    "‘Receive, then, my spirit’ (Acts 7:59). Do not let the hunters lie in wait for your sparrow (Psalm 124:7), nor let the enemies who meet me at the gates spoil my departure from the earth or trouble my ascent into the heavens.”",
    "This prayer, then, he offered up for himself; but he offered up another, in turn, for the people of the Jews: “Lord, do not set this sin against them” (Acts 7:60). And…"
  ],
  "source_text": "ψυχαὶ τῶν δικαίων εἰσέρχονται· οὐκέτι τὰ ζοφερὰ τοῦ θανάτου χωρία τὰ τῶν\nζώντων παραλαμβάνει πνεύματα. Μετὰ σὲ τῶν ζώντων ἀπαρχὴν καὶ νεκρῶν ἅμα\n5\nγενόμενον, ἵνα καὶ νεκρῶν καὶ ζώντων κυριεύσῃς, ὅλων θαρρεῖ τῶν νεκρῶν, οὐκ\nἔξω λόγου, τὸ φύραμα. «∆έξαι τοίνυν τὸ πνεῦμά μου.» Μὴ συχωρήσῃς τὸ σὸν\nστρουθίον λοχῆσαι τοῖς θηρεύουσι μηδὲ τοῖς συναντῶσιν ἐν πύλαις ἐχθροῖς τὴν\nἐμὴν ἀπὸ τῆς γῆς ἀποδημίαν λυμαίνεσθαι μηδὲ θορυβῆσαί μοι τὴν εἰς οὐρανοὺς\nἄνοδον.\n27 Ἀλλὰ ταύτην μὲν ὑπὲρ ἑαυτοῦ τὴν προσευχήν, ἑτέραν δὲ πάλιν ὑπὲρ τοῦ\nλαοῦ τῶν Ἰουδαίων ἔθυεν· «Κύριε, μὴ στήσῃς αὐτοῖς τὴν ἁμαρτίαν ταύτην.» Καὶ",
